## Error contract

- Raise / return: {{error_contract}} <!-- GEN: e.g. "subclasses of DomainError in app/shared/domain/errors.py" or "Result<T, AppError>" -->
- Translated to the outside world only at: {{error_edge}} <!-- GEN: e.g. global HTTP handler, UI error boundary -->
- Follow this contract even where generic advice differs (C11).

## Catching

- Catch the specific error you can handle; otherwise let it propagate.
- Broad catches only at {{allowed_edges}}, and always log or record them.
- Never: empty catch, `return None`/empty list on failure, retry-forever loops.

## Logging

- Logger: {{logger}}; context fields: {{log_context}}.
- No debug output left in code ({{debug_examples}}).
- Never log secrets, tokens or personal data.

